y don't require to be  equipped and in the case of the  paraglider cannot even be removed this  new system of approaching items will  most likely largely be preserved in  brief the while - with this in mind and  if we are to assume that a more  traditional approach to dungeons will  return as is being speculated and even  rumored how will the sequel handle  progression items as of right now it is  still unclear if the sheikah slay will  be a returning item in Pravda while -  neither do we  if its function will be the same or if  it will be either diminished or expanded  upon there's speculation about the  possibility of Zelda being playable  alongside link not you might be the one  to operate it but that is a topic for a  different video what we want to talk  about here is the possibilities for  progression items tools that are unique  mandatory for progression and functions  similarly to the tools found in previous  games like the hookshot hammer beetle  and more as mentioned before probe the  wise approach to progression items  differs greatly from past games so the  most likely scenario will be that the  Zelda team will present a mix between  the old and the new progression items no  longer being a standalone object that  link obtains a rod to become part of his  character which can be swapped between  using the deep the same way we switch  between the different rules of the  sheikah slate the big different this  time around being that will not be  granted all the necessary tools right at  the start rather expand their abilities  step by step as you progress through the  game and conquer its multiple dungeon  challenges this will allow for a more  traditional approach to dungeon design  with a structure unlocks bit by bit and  finally opens up completely once we  obtain the new ability found inside  dungeon notice how we call this an  ability rather than an item we believe  that this is the new way to go for off  the wild to reverting back to the  traditional Zelda items completely would  feel like a step back in the evolution  of the series thus you'll be more  fitting to go in a new direction while  at the same time borrowing from  traditional ideas the most of this  waders can be achieved full of course  buildings afflicted hands while looking  around at some of my comments one of  them posted by Zack weygers caught my  attention he makes the point that it  would be best if items like the hookshot  and claw shot are no longer treated as  physical items but rather tied to Ling's  arm and makes a strong comparison to  Darksiders - now I have never played any  of the installments from the dark side  as franchise but being the curious man  that I am I look further into it and  followed some Let's Plays of the game  and well I think he's right on the money  here as far as comparisons go I think  this might be as close as we can get in  the game the main protagonist fittingly  named death will obtain different types  of abilities that will become part of  his character the closest to home would  be the ability called the death grip  which is almost a one-on-one copy of the  grappling hook for  winwaker or the whip from skyward sword  where you can target specific objects to  cross gaps or pull smaller objects  toward you it can even be used to expand  the distance you can traverse by running  alongside walls quick note I'm totally  picking up this game before the release  of breath the wall to this game looks  freakin amazing it is said that the  developers working on the sequel are  currently being inspired by Red Dead  Redemption 2 and another unspecified  game I wouldn't even be surprised if  this turns out to be one of the  Darksiders games since Darksiders 3 came  out at the end of 2018 half a year  before the breath Mawile 2 trailer now I  know I've made this connection many  times before but it's pretty much the  only thing we have to go on as of right  now some of the concept art presented by  the zelda team seems to point into a  similar direction instead of carrying an  actual physical hammer links hand would  instead transform into a hammer shape  and wields it as if it was an actual  physical item if this is indeed  implemented most if not all progression  abilities besides the paraglider would  probably be handled in the same way  similar to how the t1000 transforms his  hands into all kinds of different  weapons and tools the next question  would be how exactly would link obtain  these new abilities  I mean it's unlikely they would be  simply lying in a chest somewhere right  the sheikah slate has a more  technological feel to it a device that  can channel different properties to  manipulate the physical world around it  like time magnetism water molecules  create blasts of energy or capture light  to create photographs the green hand  which is speculated to be tied to the  zone I seems to have a more spiritual  element to it the biggest giveaway for  this is the color of said energy green  instead of blue green of course  correlating to the luminous stones found  across Hyrule were just said to possess  the spirits of the dead as well as the  green flames and glows seen around the  deceased champions and King roam and  this does seem to make sense when  looking at the full picture the hand  that keeps the seal on Ganondorf seems  to transfer the loss of its spirit  energy the link to give him the means to  stand a chance against whatever  Ganondorf has in store for us there's a  theory that suggests that the hand was  once a full person but over the many  millennia slowly faded from existence  sacrificing its energy slowly to keep  the seal intact living only this part of  his or her body behind  now this theory would justify what link  doesn't immediately inherit all the  great powers is being once possessed and  grows into strong magic wielding warlock  which would of course be Opie to have  right at the start of the game instead  only a sliver of its full power is left 